            <ArticleTitle>Switching from CFC to HFA Inhalers: What NPs and Their Patients Need to Know.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this article is to provide nurse practitioners with a better understanding of the transition from chlorofluorocarbon (CFC) to hydrofluoralkane (HFA) metered-dose inhalers (MDIs). The authors discuss the differences in these products' propellants; the proper use, cost, and efficacy of the HFA inhalers; and the implications of the switch for NPs and for their patients with asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
